{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":370429,"duration_api_ms":256938,"ttft_ms":2558,"num_turns":30,"result":"## Summary\n\n**EXP-003: RAG few-shot** — **quality 0.320** (dev), new best (+0.013 vs baseline 0.307)\n\n**What I did:** Created `GoldExemplars.swift` with 12 hard-coded non-dev gold examples. At runtime, for each input, retrieve the 2 nearest exemplars by Jaccard word-overlap similarity and inject them as concrete few-shot demonstrations in the system prompt. Single FM call.\n\n**Result:** \n- 0.320 vs previous best 0.307 — modest but real improvement\n- First tie vs gold (learn_guitar — model asked about guitar type which gold missed)\n- Non-redundancy improved 3→4 across dev cases\n\n**Judge notes insight:** The RAG examples taught the model better redundancy avoidance, but catastrophic coverage failures persist — the model still asks \"What is the name of your bakery?\" for a naming task, and misses critical unknowns (budget for dinner party, departure city for Paris trip). The 3B model sees the good examples but still can't reliably transfer the \"which unknown is most decision-critical\" reasoning to novel task types. Next hypothesis should target this specific failure mode more aggressively (e.g., a chain-of-thought reasoning step asking \"what single fact would most change the plan?\" before generating questions).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0d29d5b9-1e74-49f2-be70-e41a5215bbde","total_cost_usd":0.47748925000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34611,"cache_read_input_tokens":438120,"output_tokens":14375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":34611},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":33611,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1000,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":14375,"cacheReadInputTokens":438120,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34611,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.47693025000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aa499a10-6382-4721-83e5-61880cc6ddf1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":482912,"duration_api_ms":219451,"ttft_ms":2050,"num_turns":21,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Experiment exp004 — `ragCoverageBestOfN`** (best-of-N RAG sets ranked by a deterministic Swift coverage scorer).\n\n- **Hypothesis:** coverage is the wall (budget/who-for/location/timeline/current-state reliably dropped). Sample N full RAG sets at varying temps, then select the best-covering one in Swift — attacking coverage with a deterministic ruler while preserving the natural phrasing of whole model-generated sets.\n- **Result: 0.245 quality (dev) — REGRESSED.** Below best (exp003 = 0.320) and baseline (0.307); spec dropped to 90% (1 error).\n- **Why it failed (honest signal):** A coverage-keyword-only ruler combined with high-temperature sampling backfires. The hotter samples introduced atomicity violations (compound/parenthetical questions) and specificity loss (US tax forms for a German task), and the scorer is blind to those, so it sometimes *selected the worse set*. Coverage itself never moved (still rubric 3).\n- **Takeaway for next time:** selection-by-proxy over the 3B's own samples is insufficient — a useful ruler must score atomicity + specificity + task-fit, not just dimension keyword presence, and sampling needs a low-temp floor. The coverage gap is still the wall; this confirms it's a *capability* limit, not a selection problem.\n\nBuild green ✅, one new run logged ✅ (`results/exp004.json`, `runs.jsonl` run #4), log line prepended to `program.md`. All edits confined to `Sources/DiscoveryAgent/` + `program.md`. Stopping here per the one-experiment rule.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b4f6d8a4-f8c2-404b-b53f-1179ef8a7dd6","total_cost_usd":0.8079705,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37084,"cache_read_input_tokens":382513,"output_tokens":15368,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":37084},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":35725,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1359,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":15368,"cacheReadInputTokens":382513,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37084,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8074115000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"dbe2f4ea-233c-4dbd-9762-44bca48bb2c0"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":311406,"duration_api_ms":167745,"ttft_ms":3470,"num_turns":17,"result":"Done. One experiment, completed and logged.\n\n**exp005 ragCritiqueRevise** — quality **0.315** (dev), spec 100%, 0 win / 1 tie / 9 loss. **DISCARDED** (−0.005 vs the exp003 best of 0.320).\n\n**What I tried:** A reflexion editor built on the current best. Stage 1 produced the strong RAG few-shot draft (= exp003); stage 2 was a second FM \"auditor\" call given that draft plus an explicit decision-critical dimension checklist (budget / who-for / timeline / scale / location / current-state / goal), instructed to delete already-given/low-value/compound questions, fill the highest-value missing unknown, and keep good questions verbatim to protect naturalness.\n\n**Why it didn't help (the honest signal):** Naturalness held (no robotic regression like the earlier pipelines), but the hard *universal* checklist backfired on coverage — the 3B auditor mechanically injected budget+timeline into tasks where they're noise (bakery naming, GP booking, German tax got \"storage budgets\"), introduced new reworded-overlap redundancy, and even produced a literal \"deadlines or deadlines.\" It swapped one set of wrong slots for another rather than supplying the task-type judgment the model lacks. Coverage stayed at 3.\n\n**Takeaway for next time:** Self-critique can't conjure judgment the base model doesn't have, and a universal checklist is too blunt. The lever should be a **task-conditioned** dimension scaffold (retrieved per task type from the gold bank) rather than reflexion or a global checklist — i.e. keep pushing on richer RAG/distillation.\n\nBuild is green; exactly one new run (`exp005`) logged to `results/runs.jsonl` and `results/exp005.json`.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e3f3e3e6-f2c8-4274-b710-054eb666e749","total_cost_usd":0.6270074999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36244,"cache_read_input_tokens":335267,"output_tokens":9286,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":36244},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":36561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1067,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":9286,"cacheReadInputTokens":335267,"cacheCreationInputTokens":36244,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6264485,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"aea31191-ef5a-48cc-94f4-df138d07a758"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":390429,"duration_api_ms":284788,"ttft_ms":3439,"num_turns":31,"result":"Done. One experiment, complete.\n\n**exp006 `ragCoverageScaffold` — quality 0.290 (dev), DISCARDED (−0.030 vs exp003 best 0.320).**\n\n- **Hypothesis:** exp005's insight said the coverage checklist must be *task-conditioned/retrieved*, not universal. So I tagged each gold question with a short decision-critical dimension label, aggregated the dimensions from the same 2 nearest exemplars exp003 retrieves, and injected them as an explicit, adaptable coverage checklist in a single call (avoiding exp005's auditor regressions).\n- **Outcome:** Build green, one new logged run (`results/exp006.json`, run #6). Coverage stayed at 3 and the headline dropped 0.030.\n- **Honest read:** A *retrieved* checklist is no better than a *universal* one. The 3B treats abstract dimension labels as slot-fillers and renders them as vague catch-all or compound questions (wedding \"date AND time\", tax \"deadlines or deadlines\", near-duplicate filed-vs-received pairs). Naming a dimension doesn't supply the judgment to pick the most-critical one or phrase it atomically — it just adds another surface to over-fit. **Both exp005 and exp006 now confirm: explicit dimension menus (universal or task-conditioned) do not fix coverage.** The next lever should inject concrete retrieved gold *questions* as harder constraints (keep/adapt N specific ones) or move to distillation/adapter — not any checklist scaffold.\n\nCurrent best remains **exp003 ragFewShot at 0.320**.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"960a385f-a193-4211-a467-6443bc203d0b","total_cost_usd":0.9879920000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39366,"cache_read_input_tokens":748851,"output_tokens":14668,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":39366},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":39514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1236,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":54,"outputTokens":14668,"cacheReadInputTokens":748851,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39366,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9874330000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"04b02476-204c-446c-a1cd-9098ca75e549"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":363582,"duration_api_ms":260814,"ttft_ms":4438,"num_turns":20,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n**Hypothesis (exp007):** exp003's win came from well-matched few-shot exemplars, but its word-overlap Jaccard retrieval returns ~0 similarity for topically distinct dev queries (resume↔interview, tax↔budget share no words). Replacing it with on-device NLEmbedding sentence-embedding cosine should surface the nearest task TYPE and lift coverage.\n\n**Implementation:** New `SemanticRetrieval.swift` (NLEmbedding cosine + Jaccard fallback), `GoldExemplars.nearestSemantic`, refactored `ragSystemPrompt` to accept overridable exemplars, new `.ragFewShotSemantic` topology, registered as `exp007`. Build green.\n\n**Result: QUALITY 0.273 (dev)** — regressed −0.047 vs the exp003 best of 0.320, and lost exp003's lone tie (now 0/0/10). Coverage stayed flat at 3.\n\n**Honest verdict: DISCARDED — hypothesis falsified.** Better-matched exemplars did not improve coverage; the same failure modes recur verbatim (misses budget/departure-city/who-for, treats tax as document-filing, near-duplicate date questions). The 3B imitates exemplar surface form, not which-unknowns-matter judgment, so topical relevance of exemplars was never the lever. This confirms (again) that retrieval/prompt-context tweaks don't move the coverage wall — pointing to the heavier untried levers (hard keep/adapt-N-gold-questions constraints, or distillation/adapter).\n\nOne new run logged (`results/exp007.json`, `runs.jsonl`), program.md updated, build green. Stopping per the one-experiment rule.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a4d45946-5640-4501-a3ce-1ff34b5b6fdf","total_cost_usd":0.8707422499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46977,"cache_read_input_tokens":532284,"output_tokens":12411,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":46977},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":47050,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1311,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":12411,"cacheReadInputTokens":532284,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46977,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.87018325,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7359fea3-a789-4f0a-ae40-f0b6010dba41"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":567501,"duration_api_ms":295668,"ttft_ms":4584,"num_turns":22,"result":"Iteration complete. One experiment run, brutally honestly assessed.\n\n## exp010 `ragSelfConsistency` — DISCARDED (quality 0.222)\n\n**Hypothesis** (grounded in exp003's per-case notes: redundancy + wasted one-off niche slots in nearly every case): the decision-critical planning unknowns are high-probability, so they recur across independent samples while idiosyncratic noise doesn't. Draw 4 independent RAG sets, embedding-cluster all 28 questions, and keep the 7 clusters with the broadest **cross-sample agreement** — a new criticality signal distinct from exp002 (self-rated importance) and exp004 (whole-set keyword scoring). Selection deterministic in Swift.\n\n**Result: 0.222** — regression of −0.098 vs the best (exp003, 0.320) and −0.085 vs baseline. Coverage actually *fell* to 2. Falsified two ways:\n1. **Dedup didn't happen.** NLEmbedding sentence cosine doesn't co-cluster paraphrases of the same unknown (\"What date?\" vs \"What time?\" land below 0.62), so the same near-duplicate pairs survived across dinner/trip/wedding/gp/etc. Embeddings rank exemplar *relevance* fine (exp007) but are too coarse to merge clarifying-question paraphrases.\n2. **Frequency surfaced filler, not criticality.** The questions that recur most are the 3B's generic catch-alls (\"any additional factors?\", \"what software are you using?\") — exactly what gold avoids. Consensus *concentrates* the model's generic tendency and drops the occasional sharp task-specific question only one sample produced. Cross-sample merging also reintroduced pronoun drift.\n\n**Insight:** you can't recover which-unknowns-matter judgment by aggregating more of the 3B's own samples — its modal output *is* the generic one. This confirms the coverage wall from a new angle and exhausts the self-consistency lever. exp003 (0.320) remains best; the only untried lever the log keeps pointing to is weight-level distillation / a LoRA adapter on the gold sets.\n\nBuild is green; run #10 logged to `results/runs.jsonl`; `program.md` updated (newest first).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5da9389c-8390-4c5a-883d-5934ac20a798","total_cost_usd":1.1004495,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52348,"cache_read_input_tokens":615861,"output_tokens":18584,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":52348},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":52536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000564,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":18584,"cacheReadInputTokens":615861,"cacheCreationInputTokens":52348,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0998855,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"769af6e8-0cef-4d6e-a3e4-16c8ed54abe9"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":255819,"duration_api_ms":152302,"ttft_ms":3129,"num_turns":14,"result":"One experiment complete. Summary:\n\n**exp011 ragContrastiveFewShot — quality 0.323 (dev)**\n\n- **Move:** Built on the best config (exp003 positive RAG few-shot, single call) and prepended one fixed GOOD-vs-BAD worked example on a neutral, non-eval task (\"Organize my garage\"). The WEAK set demonstrates exactly the judge's flagged anti-patterns (restating given facts, off-task/self-defeating, vague filler, compound, redundant). A genuinely new lever — no prior config used **negative/contrastive demonstrations**.\n- **Hypothesis:** Prior coverage fixes all added a runtime *judging* step (auditor/repair/scaffold/consensus) and regressed because the 3B can't judge; baking the judgment into a demonstration contrast might teach by example.\n- **Result:** +0.003 over exp003's 0.320 — within noise. Rubric means **identical** to exp003 across all five dimensions; coverage still pinned at 3; per-case failures recur verbatim (dinner_party misses budget+dietary, trip_paris misses departure city, resume misses existing-resume, etc.). It did suppress the catastrophic self-defeating question and held atomicity at 5, but hit the same ~0.32 plateau.\n- **Verdict:** Marginal new best by a hair, but honestly a **tie** — confirms negative demonstrations don't confer which-unknown-is-critical judgment any more than positive demos or checklists. The entire in-context family now converges at ~0.31–0.32 with coverage stuck at 3. Only untried lever left: weight-level distillation / LoRA adapter on the gold sets.\n\nBuild green, one new run logged (run #11, results/exp011.json), program.md updated.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"037e063e-ba35-47e5-82f2-2a0581c87e23","total_cost_usd":0.6689852500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42207,"cache_read_input_tokens":292395,"output_tokens":10333,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":42207},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":41758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1833,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":10333,"cacheReadInputTokens":292395,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42207,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6684262500000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f5b828bf-5f75-4f39-b038-87b38f643a27"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":566890,"duration_api_ms":155785,"ttft_ms":2280,"num_turns":19,"result":"Iteration complete. Summary:\n\n## exp012 ragTournament — DISCARDED (quality 0.297)\n\n**What I did:** The prior invocation left `exp012` (a smart pairwise best-of-N tournament) fully coded but never built/run/logged. I completed it as the one experiment this iteration — the \"pairwise 3B comparison/tournament\" selection lever the rules explicitly endorse and that had never been run.\n\n**Mechanism:** Draw 4 independent exp003 RAG sets at temps [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] → single-elimination bracket where each match is decided by the 3B comparing two whole 7-question sets, judged in **both orderings** (two-order vote, tie→lower-temp incumbent) to damp position bias → winner returned **verbatim** (no mangling).\n\n**Result:** quality **0.297** (dev), spec 100%, 0/0/10, coverage **3**, nonRed 4. Below the exp003/exp011 plateau (0.320/0.323) and below even baseline (0.307).\n\n**Insight (logged):** Relative pairwise judgment doesn't recover coverage any more than absolute scoring (exp004) or frequency consensus (exp010). The *winning* sets still contained the exact off-task questions the comparator prompt was told to penalise (dietary questions for find_therapist/gp/trip_paris, a fake tax authority, missing budget/departure-city/existing-resume). Ranking two sets by \"which covers the decision-critical unknowns\" requires the same which-unknown-is-critical judgment the 3B lacks — relativising just asks for the missing knowledge in comparison form. This closes the **entire selection family** (absolute / frequency / pairwise). The only genuinely untried lever remains weight-level distillation / a LoRA adapter trained on the gold sets.\n\nBuild is green; exactly one new run (#13) was logged to `results/runs.jsonl` + `results/exp012.json`, and one line prepended to the program.md experiment log (corrected to the real metrics 0.297/nonRed-4 vs the stale 0.290 placeholder left in the file).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4646b6e5-3868-42bf-ac1a-5ae52dbb6936","total_cost_usd":0.8587335,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62720,"cache_read_input_tokens":421459,"output_tokens":10211,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":62720},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":35791,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2680,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":14,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000549,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":10211,"cacheReadInputTokens":421459,"cacheCreationInputTokens":62720,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8581845000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a9972201-f627-4e8b-905c-3bb8430bae1c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":347804,"duration_api_ms":204227,"ttft_ms":3427,"num_turns":19,"result":"Done. One complete autoresearch iteration.\n\n## Summary\n\n**exp013 ragPlanAssumptions** — a genuinely new lever (not selection/aggregation/critique/in-context-demo, all previously exhausted at the ~0.32 plateau).\n\n**Hypothesis:** The coverage wall is that the stock 3B can't *rank* which unknowns are decision-critical. So instead of asking it to rank, I changed the cognitive task: stage 1 drafts a *concrete plan* and surfaces the *assumptions* it was forced to commit to (to plan \"trip to Paris\" it must assume departure city/dates/budget/scale = exactly the decision-critical unknowns, grounded in the specific task). Stage 2 phrased those into 7 questions via the proven exp003 RAG scaffold.\n\n**Result: 0.245 quality, coverage dropped to 2** — falsified, and the worst RAG-derived variant. Brutally honest read: when a 3B drafts a plan it commits to *execution/logistics* detail (seating, music, paperwork, \"do you have folders?\"), so the assumptions it surfaces skew to minor logistical specifics — the low-value slots gold *avoids* — while missing the high-level fundamentals (budget, who-for, departure city, scale). The extra stage also re-introduced sanity/naturalness failures the single-call exp003 had suppressed (\"Have you owned a therapist before?\", first-person \"I\").\n\n- ✅ Green build\n- ✅ Exactly one new logged run (`results/exp013.json`, run #14 in `runs.jsonl`)\n- ✅ Old configs intact; exp013 added as a new named config\n- ✅ Logged to `program.md`, discarded (not a new best)\n\n**Best remains exp003 (0.320).** The plan/counterfactual-assumption decomposition angle is now closed. The wall: every route asking the stock 3B to generate/rank/select/aggregate/critique/plan-then-introspect lands at coverage 2-3. The one genuinely untried lever remains weight-level distillation / a LoRA adapter — which has no knob exposed in `DiscoveryConfig` yet.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dc4de993-086c-4299-ae50-d1ecd8787ab8","total_cost_usd":0.8473085,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41316,"cache_read_input_tokens":501039,"output_tokens":13513,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":41316},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":40999,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1701,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":13513,"cacheReadInputTokens":501039,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41316,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8467495,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":479,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000559,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a6627a42-df6c-4fbf-9788-88f338e00f4c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":341102,"duration_api_ms":215710,"ttft_ms":2730,"num_turns":18,"result":"Done. One complete autoresearch iteration:\n\n**exp015 `ragDimensionalSchema`** — a genuinely new lever (guided-schema design, untried — every prior config emitted one flat `questions: [FMQuestion].count(7)` array). Replaced the flat array with **seven distinctly-`@Guide`d typed slots**, one per universal high-value planning dimension (goal/scope/who-for/budget/timeline/current-state/constraints), so guided generation *structurally enforces* coverage breadth rather than relying on the 3B to rank which unknown is critical.\n\n**Result: QUALITY 0.243 (dev), spec 100%, 0/0/10, coverage still 3 — DISCARDED** (−0.077 vs the exp003/exp011 ~0.32 plateau, −0.064 vs baseline).\n\n**Honest verdict:** falsified, and it actively regressed. Forcing a *fixed universal* dimension set is exp005/006's mechanical-checklist injection made rigid — it guaranteed breadth of *generic* dimensions but crowded out the *task-specific* critical ones. The judge notes confirm the mechanism exactly: a budget slot injected into bakery-naming/GP/resume, a low-value \"who is the wedding for?\", odd meta asks (\"how many concepts to explore?\"), vague \"things to avoid\" catch-alls, and rigid slots *replacing* the real unknowns (trip_paris asked about a booked flight instead of departure city; therapist lost location/modality). A dimension being universally common ≠ decision-critical for *this* task.\n\n- Build: green ✅\n- New logged run: exp015 (run #16) ✅\n- Logged to `program.md` with the insight that this closes the structural-schema lever; the wall now holds across the entire prompting/topology/post-processing space, leaving only the (not-yet-available) LoRA adapter.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6ef58eb5-2641-4da9-ae3c-a5305f8929c8","total_cost_usd":1.053548,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":62692,"ca